  "id": "cognitiveaffective-personality-system",
  "term": "cognitive–affective personality system",
  "definition": "The cognitive–affective personality system is a theory used to explain how a situation can trigger a chain of mental and emotional responses that shape later motivation and behavior. In this account, situational cues activate a person’s appraisals, which are then linked to outcomes such as engagement and performance.",
